  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<b><color=#FBBF24>THE IDEA</color></b>

    The pallets are the <b>frames</b>
    of physical memory, the numbered boxes are <b>pages</b>. Load the pages in the
    order of the reference string. When every frame is full, the algorithm picks
    the victim: <b>FIFO</b> the oldest, <b>LRU</b> the least recently used, <b>Optimal</b>
    the one needed furthest in the future.


    <b><color=#FBBF24>CONTROLS</color></b>

    <b>Headset</b> 
    grab a box with the grip (close by, or point at it) and let go of it on a frame''s
    pallet, or just in front of the rack below it. A wrong frame sends the box back
    to its table. Press the screens with the ray (trigger).

    <b>Desktop</b> 
    WASD walk, mouse look, <b>E</b> or click a box to pick it up, then a pallet to
    put it there.

    <b>Phone</b>  drag to look, two fingers to walk, tap a box,
    then a pallet.

    <b>Headset</b>  left stick walk, right stick turn (push up
    to teleport). Look at a controller to see its buttons.

    <b>Hands</b>  point
    + pinch to select; pinch the ground and release to teleport; pinch + flick sideways
    to turn; left palm up for MENU.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
