  m_IsActive: 1
--- !u!114 &1164072312
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1164072311}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 778b0a6312cb7b11bafe17d431fc4896, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MemoryTour
  steps:
  - id: mem_welcome
    title: Welcome to the warehouse
    text: Welcome to the memory warehouse. A program is split into pages, but physical
      memory only has room for a few of them at a time.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a90efba5255a5673c9fe5b2ced75ee5b, type: 3}
  - id: mem_frames
    title: Frames
    text: The three pallets on the rack are the frames of physical memory. Each frame
      holds exactly one page.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c0479a532843352d89122d930cf059a4, type: 3}
  - id: mem_pages
    title: Pages
    text: The numbered boxes are the program's pages. The program asks for them in
      a fixed order, called the reference string, shown on the screen.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4fff4afe24878cfaab4d09629850a916, type: 3}
  - id: mem_algorithm
    title: Replacement policy
    text: 'When every frame is full and a new page is needed, one page must leave.
      The policy decides which. Let''s start with FIFO: first in, first out.'
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7eee8c4ff9cedd4b69bc9ae7bb9882d3, type: 3}
  - id: mem_turn
    title: Your turn
    text: 'Your turn. Load the page the screen asks for: pick up its box, then put
      it on an empty pallet.'
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 11d0909aa1a7fe549934a75e274ad745, type: 3}
  - id: mem_hint
    title: Hint
    text: Look at the screen for the next page number. Pick up that box, and place
      it on any empty pallet.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a8b12e430bece5f72acfa27d84203253, type: 3}
  - id: mem_fault
    title: Page fault
    text: 'That was a page fault: the page was not in memory, so it had to be brought
      in. Keep loading pages in order. Soon all three frames will be full.'
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f27e42e806b56c5d5bdc105ef35ed1c9, type: 3}
  - id: mem_victim
    title: Who leaves?
    text: Memory was full, so FIFO sent away the page that came in first. LRU would
      evict the page unused the longest, and Optimal the one needed furthest in the
      future.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 96a4df5b669ccfb8b8139acb85c4e450, type: 3}
  - id: mem_outro
    title: Compare the policies
    text: Finish the string, then try LRU and Optimal on the screen and compare the
      number of faults. Fewer faults means a faster program.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d21793114f61b9899a022d819705ec53, type: 3}
